_Rule_in_the_Nineteenth_Century","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL39702885M/Muslims_under_Sikh_Rule_in_the_Nineteenth_Century","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL9577733A","name":"Robina Yasmin"}],"isbn_13":["9780755640362"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"200","publish_date":"2023","publishers":["I. B. Tauris & Company, Limited"],"source_records":["bwb:9780755640362"],"title":"Muslims under Sikh Rule in the Nineteenth Century","weight":"0.455","subtitle":"Maharaja Ranjit Singh and Religious Tolerance","full_title":"Muslims under Sikh Rule in the Nineteenth Century Maharaja Ranjit Singh and Religious Tolerance","works":[{"key":"/works/OL25328282W"}],"key":"/books/OL39702885M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-09-18T23:54:23.832020"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-09-18T23:54:23.832020"}}},"ISBN:9780755640324":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780755640324","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL33926077M/Muslims_under_Sikh_Rule_in_the_Nineteenth_Century","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL33926077M/Muslims_under_Sikh_Rule_in_the_Nineteenth_Century","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL9577733A","name":"Robina Yasmin"}],"isbn_13":["9780755640324"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"number_of_pages":224,"publish_date":"2022","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9780755640324","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:39386601:3568"],"title":"Muslims under Sikh Rule in the Nineteenth Century","subtitle":"Maharaja Ranjit Singh and Religious Tolerance","works":[{"key":"/works/OL25328282W"}],"key":"/books/OL33926077M","lc_classifications":["DS485.P87 Y26 2022eb"],"oclc_numbers":["1290487445"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Though the history of Sikh-Muslim relations is fraught with conflict, this book examines how the policies of Sikh rulers attempted to avoid religious bigotry and prejudice at a time when Muslims were treated as third-class citizens. Focusing on the socio-economic, political and religious condition of Muslims under Sikh rule in the Punjab during the 19th century, this book demonstrates that Maharaja Ranjit Singh and his successors took a secular approach towards their subjects. Using various archival sources, including the Fakir Khana Family archives and the Punjab Archives, the author argues citizens had freedom to practice their religion, with equal access to employment, education and justice\"--"},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9780755640355"]},"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-28T11:10:31.426082"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-04-30T12:35:56.231651"}}},"ISBN:9780674258518":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780674258518","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34779945M/Poems_from_the_Guru_Granth_Sahib","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34779945M/Poems_from_the_Guru_Granth_Sahib","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7641899A","name":"Guru Nanak"},{"key":"/authors/OL834777A","name":"Nikky-Guninder Kaur Singh"}],"isbn_13":["9780674258518"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"},{"key":"/languages/pan"}],"lc_classifications":["BL2017.4.A32 2022","BL2017.4 .A32 2022"],"publish_date":"2022","publishers":["Harvard University Press"],"source_records":["bwb:9780674258518","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-032.mrc:220022941:3152","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_033.bib.mrc:107393827:4146"],"subjects":["Religion"],"title":"Poems from the Guru Granth Sahib","weight":"0.666","pagination":"624","works":[{"key":"/works/OL25800100W"}],"key":"/books/OL34779945M","lccn":["2021014845"],"oclc_numbers":["1240492767"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Guru Nanak (1469-1539), a native of Panjab, founded the Sikh religion. His vast corpus of nearly a thousand hymns forms the core of the Guru Granth Sahib, the Sikhs' sacred book of ethics, philosophy, and theology. The scripture was expanded and enriched by his nine successors, and Sikhs continue to revere it today as the embodiment of their tradition. Poems from the Guru Granth Sahib offer a compilation of spiritual lyrics showcasing the range and depth of Guru Nanak's literary style while conveying his pluralistic vision of the singular divine and his central values of equality, inclusivity, and civic action. This new English translation includes celebrated long hymns such as \"Alphabet on the Board\" and \"Ballad of Hope\" alongside innovative shorter poems like \"The Hours.\" It is presented here alongside the original text in Gurmukhi, the script developed by the Guru himself\"--"},"latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-08T00:40:20.399090"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-03-21T19:54:38.321370"}}}}